<title>USA: Wilshire Oil well tests at 324 bbls/day.</title>
<headline>Wilshire Oil well tests at 324 bbls/day.</headline>
<dateline>JERSEY CITY, N.J. 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wilshire Oil Co of Texas said on Friday that its Edwards 3-12 discovery well in Ochiltree County, Texas, produced the equivalent of 324 barrels per day in initial tests.</p>
<p>Wilshire, which has a 50 percent working interest in the well, said Edwards 3-12 tested with a tubing pressure of 200 pounds per square inch and a casing pressure of 500 pounds per square inch.</p>
<p>The well is producing from the Oswego formation at 6,900 feet, Wilshire said.</p>
</text>
